  "description": "For 2019, the Solum i/O ST brings Haro's vaunted Rider Tuned Geometry to the pedelec category in a gender neutral step thru option that allows an easy dismount alternative when sweeping your leg around he back isn't desired or possible. Regardless of conventional or step thru, each is designed from the ground up to be the ultimate sporty eBike, the Solum i/O ST is equally at home crushing your commute, unpaved lake roads, or that rails to trails route on the weekend. Shimano's STePS e6100 center-drive motor system provides assistance up to 20 miles per hour, and its 418eH battery provides you with up to a 60 mile range depending on mode selected. Shimano's 1x10 drivetrain is simple and efficient and allows you to get from here to there without even breaking a sweat. Solum i/O ST has full rack and fender mounts, Haro commuter saddle with a micro adjust seat post, and Shimano MT-200 hydraulic brakes that provide reliable stops in all weather conditions.\nLightweight 6061 aluminum i/O-specific frame with Haro's proven Rider Tuned Geometry\nSmooth Shimano STePS e6100 motor w/418eH battery for up to 60 mile range\nSR Suntour NEX HLO suspension fork with 63mm travel and hydraulic lockout\nShimano 10-spd Deore drivetrain\nNew Pivit alloy 9* sweep riser bar, and forged stem\nShimano MT201 hydraulic disc brakes\nFast-rolling Kenda Kwick Drumlin 700c X 38mm all-purpose tires\nNew Pivit alloy 9* sweep riser bar, and forged stem\nReady for anything with an alloy rack & fenders\nFront and rear lights",
